---
pre-compare: sort
---
from {i: 1}, {i: 2}
// The print_json DETERMINISM question, pinned head-on instead of assumed:
// two records with the same content in opposite key insertion order at
// every nesting level, built by conditional assignment because a read_json
// batch unifies same-shaped records into one schema layout — the
// divergence this test exists for would never reach the operator through a
// shared fixture file. The read-back lane cannot reproduce field order
// anyway (ClickHouse sorts the keys of stored JSON values;
// reference/operators/from_clickhouse.md), so attest's
// print_json(this.sort()) must be insertion-order-independent for the
// verify recompute to ever match. The asserts make the proof
// load-bearing: the first fails if print_json alone were already
// canonical (the pair would no longer be a discriminating fixture), the
// second if sort()+print_json is not deterministic over identical
// content.
if i == 1 {
  this = {
    activity_id: 1,
    assignee: {name: "hermes-agent"},
    category_uid: 2,
    class_uid: 2005,
    desc: "determinism probe: same content, different key insertion order",
    finding_info_list: [{
      created_time: 2026-10-17T09:00:00Z,
      related_events: null,
      title: "Determinism probe",
      uid: "case-determinism",
    }],
    metadata: {
      correlation_uid: "case-determinism",
      product: {name: "homelab-investigations", vendor_name: "apocrathia", version: "0.1.0"},
      profiles: [],
      uid: "determinism-probe",
      version: "1.9.0",
    },
    severity_id: 3,
    status_id: 1,
    time: 2026-10-17T09:00:00Z,
    type_uid: 200501,
  }
} else {
  this = {
    type_uid: 200501,
    time: 2026-10-17T09:00:00Z,
    status_id: 1,
    severity_id: 3,
    metadata: {
      version: "1.9.0",
      uid: "determinism-probe",
      profiles: [],
      product: {version: "0.1.0", vendor_name: "apocrathia", name: "homelab-investigations"},
      correlation_uid: "case-determinism",
    },
    finding_info_list: [{
      uid: "case-determinism",
      title: "Determinism probe",
      related_events: null,
      created_time: 2026-10-17T09:00:00Z,
    }],
    desc: "determinism probe: same content, different key insertion order",
    class_uid: 2005,
    category_uid: 2,
    assignee: {name: "hermes-agent"},
    activity_id: 1,
  }
}
homelab::investigations::ocsf::attest
// Post-attest plumbing: the operator already fingerprinted from
// this.sort(), so these assignments cannot perturb the proof.
_unsorted = print_json(this)
_fp = attestation_list[0].fingerprint.value
lag value=_unsorted, into=_prev_unsorted
lag value=_fp, into=_prev_fp
where _prev_unsorted? != null
insertion_order_sensitive = _unsorted != _prev_unsorted
fingerprints_identical = _fp == _prev_fp
assert insertion_order_sensitive, message="print_json is insertion-order sensitive; the fixture pair must differ in key order for this test to have teeth"
assert fingerprints_identical, message="sorted-key serialization must fingerprint identical content identically regardless of key insertion order"
drop _unsorted, _prev_unsorted, _fp, _prev_fp
